            <ArticleTitle>Depression, stress, and coronary heart disease: the need for more complex models.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>419-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Depression has been related both to the development of coronary heart disease and to prognosis in patients following acute myocardial infarction, but the clinical significance of these associations remains uncertain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
